# Agent Instructions

`{{ .name }}` is an Intropy extractor: a run-to-completion .NET 10 job that
{{- if eq .source "sql" }}
reads the rows after its watermark from its source port's database once per
run and publishes them as one `{{ .publishes }}` message.
{{- else }}
sweeps its source port once per run and publishes each file as the
`{{ .publishes }}` message.
{{- end }}

## Project overview

- App id: `{{ .appId }}`
- Message: `{{ .publishes }}` (also the CloudEvents type)
- CloudEvent source: `{{ if .eventSource }}{{ .eventSource }}{{ else }}{{ .eventSourceValue }}{{ end }}`
- Topic: `{{ .channel }}`, declared in `.intropy/scaffold.json`. The code
  publishes on `INTROPY_PUBSUB_NAME` / `INTROPY_TOPIC_NAME`, which the system
  host and the deployment set.
{{- if eq .source "sql" }}
- Source port: `{{ .port }}`, an external port (`PortRef.DefineExternal` in the
  system host's `Ports.cs`): a SQL query, no Dapr binding
- Query: `src/Sql/Query.sql`, embedded; the watermark column is `ChangeId`
  (`Delta.Column` in `Composition.cs`)
- Payload type: `{{ .payloadType }}` in the sibling `../{{ .contracts }}` project;
  the shape of a read's rows `Source{{ .payloadType }}` stays in `src/Model/`
- Exit codes: `0` success, `1` a read failed and its range stays pending,
  `2` sidecar unavailable
- Config keys (`src/appsettings*.json`):
  - `Ports:{{ .port }}:Kind`: `Sql` (SQL Server); `Sqlite` in Development
  - `Ports:{{ .port }}:ConnectionString`: a secret; Development reads
    `{{ .appId }}.db`, and the system host's development settings override it
  - `Ports:{{ .port }}:InitialWatermark`: `int:0`, the watermark before the
    first run
  - `Ports:{{ .port }}:CursorStore`: the state store the watermark is kept in,
    `{{ .cursorStore }}`; the system host and the deployment set it
{{- else }}
- Source port: `{{ .port }}`, declared in the system host's `Ports.cs`
- Payload type: `{{ .payloadType }}` in the sibling `../{{ .contracts }}` project;
  the source file shape `Source{{ .payloadType }}` stays in `src/Model/`
- Exit codes: `0` success, `1` a file failed and was left in place,
  `2` sidecar unavailable
- Config keys (`src/appsettings*.json`):
  - `Ports:{{ .port }}:Kind`: `Local` in Development; a deployment sets
    `Ports__{{ .port }}__Kind` (`Sftp`, `AzureBlob`)
{{- end }}
  - `PlatformServices:IdempotencyServiceAppId`: `{{ .idempotencyAppId }}`
  - `PlatformServices:BusinessIncidentServiceAppId`: `{{ .businessIncidentsAppId }}`

## Important files

{{- if eq .source "sql" }}

- `src/Composition/Composition.cs`: DI registrations, the SQL source's query
  and delta (`ConfigureSource`), and the `AddExtractor` sources, routes and
  pipeline (`ConfigurePipeline`, with source idempotency on the read's range).
  `{{ .name }}.Composition` is both a namespace and a class, so nested
  namespaces call `Composition.Composition`.
{{- else }}

- `src/Composition/Composition.cs`: DI registrations and the `AddExtractor`
  sources, routes and pipeline (`ConfigurePipeline`, with the idempotency id
  and date extractors). `{{ .name }}.Composition` is both a namespace and a
  class, so nested namespaces call `Composition.Composition`.
{{- end }}
- `src/Constants.cs`: component name, source port, CloudEvent source and type.
- `src/Process/`: the pipeline steps (`Deserializer`, `Validator`, `Transformer`).
- `test/{{ .name }}.Test.Unit/`: step unit tests.
{{- if eq .source "sql" }}
- `test/{{ .name }}.Test.Integration/`: watermark (`SqlSweepTests`), publish
  and composition tests against a SQLite file and `Intropy.Framework.Testing`
  fakes (in `FakeEdges.cs`). `SqlSweepTests` creates the table
  `Sql/Query.sql` reads; change them together.
{{- else }}
- `test/{{ .name }}.Test.Integration/`: sweep, publish and composition tests
  on `Intropy.Framework.Testing` fakes (fakes in `FakeEdges.cs`).
{{- end }}
- `Dockerfile`, `Dockerfile.dockerignore`: image build. The build context is
  the system folder: `docker build -f {{ .appId }}/Dockerfile -t {{ .appId }} .`

## Build and test

The extractor runs via its system host, which runs it once at startup and
provides the {{ if eq .source "sql" }}cursor store{{ else }}source binding{{ end }}, the pub/sub and the platform services.

```bash
task build
task test        # or task test:unit / task test:integration
task coverage    # Cobertura report under the integration project's TestResults/
```

## Development notes
{{ if eq .source "sql" }}
- The step bodies and the serializer's subject/time throw
  `NotImplementedException`; `task test` is red until they are implemented,
  except the tests that exercise only the query and the watermark.
- The model and the unit tests' inputs are empty shells; give them the shape
  of `Sql/Query.sql`'s rows.
{{- else if .empty }}
- The step bodies and the idempotency id/date extractors throw
  `NotImplementedException`; `task test` is red until they are implemented.
  The business-incident, duplicate-cancel and delete-failure sweep tests are
  not scaffolded; add them with the implementation.
{{- else }}
- Idempotency keys off the order's `OrderId` / `OrderDate`, which are also the
  CloudEvent `Subject` / `Time`.
- The `Validator` fails with `Retriable: false`: invalid data routes a
  business incident and the file is consumed.
{{- end }}

## Framework guidance

Framework how-to (pipelines, blocks, endpoints, Dapr components, testing) lives in the Intropy documentation at <https://docs.intropy.io>. For CLI facts, read `intropy template show` and `intropy <command> --help` at the moment you need them; template releases change.
